# Headers Cloudflare attaches to static assets, including the ones the Worker
# serves through the ASSETS binding. That is what makes this worth having:
# the caching below applies without giving up the Worker in front of it (see
# the run_worker_first note in wrangler.jsonc).
#
# Vite writes a content hash into every filename under /assets/, so those URLs
# cannot change meaning: a new build is a new name. They were going out as
# `max-age=0, must-revalidate`, so a browser asked again for every chunk on
# every page load, and each of those was a request for a file that could not
# have changed.
#
# X-Content-Type-Options is the only part of the security baseline repeated
# here. The rest of it (CSP, Referrer-Policy, Permissions-Policy) governs
# documents rather than subresources, and still arrives from
# applySecurityHeaders in src/worker/security-headers.ts; a second copy of the
# CSP is a second copy to keep in step.

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
